meta {
  name: 01_WHEN_RemovingAnAltinn2RoleThatIsNotHeld
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accessmanagement/api/v1/enduser/connections/roles?party={{party}}&from={{party}}&to={{to}}&rolecode=a0212
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  party: {{party}}
  from: {{party}}
  to: {{to}}
  rolecode: a0212
}

docs {
  WHEN the delegator removes an Altinn 2 role the receiver does not hold.

  `DELETE /accessmanagement/api/v1/enduser/connections/roles?party={party}&from={from}&to={to}&rolecode={code}`

  Removes a role assignment from `from` to `to` that was imported from Altinn 2. Only
  roles provided by Altinn 2 can be removed this way; Altinn 3 roles (rightholder, agent)
  and roles from the Central Coordinating Register (daglig leder and the like) are
  rejected. When the role is not assigned the call changes nothing and still returns 204,
  so it is safe to repeat.

  - Query: `party` (required), the uuid of the acting party, which must be `from` (giver
    side, to others) or `to` (receiver side, from others); `from` and `to` (required),
    the uuids of the two parties; `rolecode` (required), the Altinn 3 code of the role,
    for example `a0212` (Primary industry and foodstuff), case insensitive.
  - Token: personal token with `altinn:portal/enduser`, or
    `altinn:accessmanagement/enduser:connections:toothers.write` when party is `from` and
    `...:fromothers.write` when party is `to`; the user must have write access to access
    management (`altinn_access_management`) for the party.
  - Responses: 204 with no body; 400 AM-00039 for an unknown role code; 400 AM-00040 when
    the role cannot be revoked here (not an Altinn 2 role, or held only through another
    connection); 403 when the user cannot act for the party.
}

script:pre-request {
  const { loginAs, testdata } = require("./test/EnduserAPI/Connections/AvailableUsersAndRights/helpers.js");
  const td = testdata();

  bru.setVar("party", td.delegator.partyUuid);
  bru.setVar("to", td.receiver.partyUuid);

  await loginAs(td.delegator);
}

tests {
  test("THEN removing a role that is not held returns 204 with no body", function() {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(204);
  });
}
